title Caravan arrange -- a plan may be written in any order, and the queue seats it
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, condense REMEMBER, send the increment
think Standfast first. Every living row in crux/REDS.md -- 80, 83, 84, 85 -- carries a closure note, and the prose notes 81, 82, 85-reopened, 86, 87 all read Released. Nothing agent-closable stands open, so the line was clear for constructive work.
think Council rota by lap index -- 475 .kyri logs on disk, this is lap 476, and 476 mod 27 = 17, so the deep-read was context/LEXICON.md. Its opening line governs the whole tree's naming: each name teaches its function. That read straight into this rung's word. The queue does not sort, order, or topologically-sort a plan; it seats one -- arrange is the plain warm verb a newcomer grasps at once, and it stands beside precede, mask, fence, and phases without borrowing any of their senses.
think The running thread came from the newest log's recommend: every reading in the arc takes the queue's written order as given and only ever loosens or tightens which pairs may be swapped, so a plan whose turns are written in an order no author intended is kept faithfully in the wrong order. The honest crux was whether the queue may derive its own head order from the names already written.
think Reading precede.rye showed the gap is sharper than the recommend named it. The supervisor admits its head unconditionally -- items_contend is asked only for passes -- so a plan whose sequence contradicts its own turn names does not merely run in a suboptimal order: it runs into the fill_table invariant that says a preceded reading never runs a phase past a turn its turn named. The failure was a panic mid-flight with children already started, which is the least safe shape a refusal can take.
think So the rung has two halves rather than one. The door half: a plan is seated when no phase stands before a phase of a turn it names, checked in one bounded pass over pairs before provisioning, answering PlanUnseated with zero children started. The derivation half: every fact that check needs is already written down, so arrange seats the earliest-written phase nothing unseated still holds and derives the lawful order rather than asking an author to have typed one.
think Direction carried the termination proof for free, the same way it carried the closing in precede. A turn names only turns numbered below it, and a turn's steps keep their written order, so among the unseated phases the one with the smallest turn number -- earliest written on a tie -- is held by nothing. No visited set, no back-tracking, no second pass. The stall refusal (PlanUnseatable) is kept as a named answer rather than an assert, so an unsound caller hears why.
think The supervisor itself is asked rather than restated -- run_queue delegates to precede.run_queue after the door, so every number this rung reports stands beside every rung before it unconverted, and the module is 368 lines of door rather than another copy of the table machinery. That is the TAME reflex (ask, do not restate) paying directly in review surface.
think Stability is what makes the derived order honest. Seating the earliest-written free phase means two phases neither of which holds the other keep the sequence they were handed, so a seating moves a phase only where a name demands it. Over the elder lap that recovers the hand-written order exactly, which is the finding worth measuring.
obs The arranged run recovers the hand-written run measure for measure -- 1 pass against 1, 6 slots unspent against 6, 0 named turns broken, 7 children to the same end, peak in flight and out_of_mask equal by assert. The claim is not that the seating is good enough; it is that the seating is the order an author would have had to write out by hand.
obs Arranging moves phases and never touches a name -- the seating reads the closed plan, so a turn inherits every order it reaches through another, and writes out the original, so the arranged plan carries no name its author never typed. plans_match proves the permutation phase for phase.
obs A seated plan arranges to itself exactly, which is this arc's standing generalization test -- an empty turn mask was the sibling mask, a full sibling mask was the fence and the link, and now the identity holds one tier further out.
obs The cost is named rather than hidden. Arranging buys back no slot and refuses no pass; what it buys is that an author no longer has to write the lawful order, and it costs one bounded seating at the door -- max_seating_tests is stated as max_queue_len squared rather than left for a reader to work out. Safety first, then the slot, in TAME order.
obs Both RED paths proven on metal before GREEN was claimed. Removing the door check made the elder invariant fire at caravan/precede.rye:615 with children already in flight, which is exactly the failure the door prevents; hiding the turn mask from the seating made the pure read red at the derived order failing to recover the one the author wrote, caught in the happy zone before a single child starts.
obs A two-step turn earns its place in the pure room. Turns of one phase can never show that a seating keeps a turn's steps in written order, so the small two_step_queue puts a two-step turn behind the turn that names it and proves both steps move forward together, in sequence.
loom witness=caravan_arrange_witness rings=35 phases=7 passes_hand=1 passes_arranged=1 slots_unspent_hand=6 slots_unspent_arranged=6 children=7 refused_children=0 out_of_precede=0
file caravan/arrange.rye the rung -- the seating claim, the derivation, and a door that refuses a plan its own names forbid before any child starts
file tools/caravan_arrange_witness.rish the witness on metal -- both RED paths named, checks read natively via contains per the apostrophe loom
file caravan/README.md the durable prose for the rung, appended in the same commit as the code it describes
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge moved to arrange, precede folded into the prior-edges pointer, ring count thirty-four to thirty-five
recommend keep-going the honest next crux is what the queue still cannot say about a plan it has already seated -- every rung in this arc reasons over a queue handed whole before the first child starts, so work that arrives while the supervisor is already running has no door at all, and the question becomes whether a phase may join a plan mid-flight without the seating being redone or the orders already granted being disturbed, which wants a lap measuring what an admission costs against a re-seating
